KZ2 patch 7010: KZ2_LL_PROF=1, where the lock-line stripes are waited for and held, by call site.

An earlier change's host profile put about 30 % of Gfx.Particles.UpdateJob's samples in the runtime's lock-line path
(spu_ll_lock_slow 9.2 %, coherence notify 5.8 %). Which caller waits, and which one holds a stripe long, the profile
cannot say: spu_ll_lock_slow is one function for every site. With KZ2_LL_PROF=1 spu_ll_lock_mask and
spu_lockline_lock key each call by their return address and count calls, contended calls, stripes, the TSC ticks
spent acquiring and the ticks held until the thread's matching unlock; GETLLAR's seqlock spins (a writer holding the
line's stripe) are counted apart. "[ll-prof]" lines every 10 s (RVAs in the exe: resolve with nm). Off by default
(one env lookup); no behaviour change.
An earlier change: the 10 s print check looked at time() on every unlock; under Wine time() is GetTimeZoneInformation ->
NtQuerySystemInformation, a system call, and that was an earlier change's "86 % of UpdateJob's samples in a blocked system
call" (named with patch 7011's caller chains). The clock is now read once per 4096 unlocks per thread.

